1
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:12,060
A delivery robot in a warehouse can only move along the grid lines.

2
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:14,030
It starts at negative 3, 2.

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,960
It must reach 5, 2.

4
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:18,020
How far does the robot travel?

5
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:21,600
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,310
Count along the grid.

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:26,060
From negative 3 to 0 is 3 squares.

8
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:27,850
From 0 to 5 is 5 more.

9
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,940
That makes 8 units.

10
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:32,980
Remember: in a coordinate pair, x comes first.

11
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:35,230
x is across, and left is negative.

12
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,760
y is up, and down is negative.

13
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:40,100
A and B have the same y coordinate.

14
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,860
So they lie on a horizontal line.

15
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:47,790
The distance between them is the difference of the x coordinates.

16
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:50,160
5 minus negative 3 is 8.

17
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:53,550
Subtracting a negative is the same as adding.

18
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,150
5 plus 3 is 8.

19
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,770
Next, the robot goes from B to C: from 5, 2 down to 5, negative 4.

20
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:04,860
These points have the same x coordinate, so the line is vertical.

21
00:01:04,910 --> 00:01:08,870
The distance is the difference of the y coordinates.

22
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,260
2 minus negative 4 is 6.

23
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:16,020
So the whole journey is 8 plus 6, which is 14 units.

24
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:16,780
Your turn.

25
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:20,420
What is the distance from 1, 4 to 1, negative 5?

26
00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:23,860
Pause the video and try it.

27
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:28,540
The x coordinates are the same, so subtract the y coordinates.

28
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:30,350
4 minus negative 5 is 9.

29
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,710
The distance is 9 units.

30
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,050
Here is the method.

31
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,060
Step 1: check which coordinate is the same.

32
00:01:37,110 --> 00:01:39,030
The same y means horizontal.

33
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:41,400
The same x means vertical.

34
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:46,920
Step 2: subtract the other coordinates: the larger minus the smaller.

35
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:51,540
Step 3: remember that subtracting a negative is adding.

36
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:52,600
Step 4: check.

37
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:55,340
A distance is never negative.

38
00:01:55,390 --> 00:02:01,600
Find the distance from P, at negative 2, negative 6, to Q, at negative 2, 5.

39
00:02:01,650 --> 00:02:06,840
The x coordinate is negative 2 both times, so the line is vertical.

40
00:02:06,890 --> 00:02:09,140
5 minus negative 6 is 11.

41
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:12,000
The distance is 11 units.

42
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:13,680
R is at negative 4, 3.

43
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:16,140
S is 10 units to the right of R.

44
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:17,230
Find S.

45
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,160
Moving right adds to the x coordinate.

46
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,020
Negative 4 plus 10 is 6.

47
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:25,040
The y coordinate stays the same.

48
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:27,380
So S is at 6, 3.

49
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:28,100
Your turn.

50
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:30,530
T is 6 units below the point 3, 2.

51
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:32,680
What is the y coordinate of T?

52
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:36,010
Pause the video and try it.

53
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:39,470
Moving down subtracts from the y coordinate.

54
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,360
2 minus 6 is negative 4.

55
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:43,640
T is at 3, negative 4.

56
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:47,620
A rectangle has corners at negative 2, negative 3.

57
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:49,140
Then 4, negative 3.

58
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:49,930
Then 4, 1.

59
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:51,370
And negative 2, 1.

60
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:54,470
Find its perimeter and its area.

61
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:57,890
The width is 4 minus negative 2, which is 6.

62
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:01,940
The height is 1 minus negative 3, which is 4.

63
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:08,680
For the perimeter, add the width and the height, then double: 2 times 10 is 20 units.

64
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:13,030
The area is 6 times 4, which is 24 square units.

65
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:17,990
Find the point halfway between negative 6, 2 and 4, 2.

66
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,170
The distance is 4 minus negative 6, which is 10.

67
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:24,110
Half of 10 is 5.

68
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,500
Move 5 right from negative 6.

69
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:29,140
Negative 6 plus 5 is negative 1.

70
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:32,570
The halfway point is negative 1, 2.

71
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,920
Find the distance from negative 5, 1 to 3, 1.

72
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:37,630
Here is Otto's working.

73
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:40,260
Which line goes wrong first?

74
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:41,470
Line 1 is wrong.

75
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:45,370
The first x coordinate is negative 5, not 5.

76
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,190
3 minus negative 5 is 8.

77
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,010
The distance is 8 units.

78
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:52,450
You can check by counting on the grid.

79
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,520
A lift works like a vertical number line.

80
00:03:55,570 --> 00:04:02,670
From floor negative 2, in the car park, up to floor 9, is 9 minus negative 2: 11 floors.

81
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:06,130
In chess, a rook moves only along rows and columns.

82
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:10,140
Its moves are exactly the distances in this lesson.

83
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:16,590
And in a city built on a grid, you count blocks across, and blocks up, in just the same way.

84
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,960
One last question.

85
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:22,280
What is the distance from negative 7, 0 to negative 2, 0?

86
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:25,730
Pause the video and answer.

87
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:29,580
Larger minus smaller: negative 2 minus negative 7.

88
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:33,520
That is negative 2 plus 7, which is 5 units.

89
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:36,810
To remember: the same y means a horizontal line.

90
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:39,830
The distance is the difference in x.

91
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,060
The same x means a vertical line.

92
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:45,040
The distance is the difference in y.

93
00:04:45,090 --> 00:04:47,380
Take the larger minus the smaller.

94
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:50,190
Subtracting a negative is adding.

95
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,750
Distances are never negative.

96
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:58,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.2 on Camday.
